.DS_store
.vscode
.venv/
.idea/
.junie/
.ruff_cache/

# Generated trees that show up in `git status` on every branch, because they are
# left on disk by whichever branch last built them.
#
# Deliberately NOT `launcher/` wholesale: that path is tracked on `rust-main`
# (package.json, README.md, src-tauri sources), so ignoring the directory would
# hide real code the moment anyone works there. Only the generated children are
# listed. None of these paths has ever been tracked on any branch -- checked
# with `git log --all -- <path>` before adding them.
launcher/node_modules/
launcher/build/
launcher/src-tauri/gen/
launcher/.svelte-kit/

# Agent scratch space and per-machine settings. `worktrees/` is where isolated
# agent checkouts live and runs to gigabytes; `settings.local.json` is local by
# name and by nature. Anything under `.claude/` that IS meant to be shared --
# agent or skill definitions, for instance -- stays trackable, which is why this
# is not a blanket `.claude/`.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Gate captures. `docker compose config` output, taken from a live server so a
# test can diff the real thing against the fixture -- see 7.2's runbook, which
# feeds it back through `YULON_COMPOSE_CONFIG`. Per-run and per-machine: the
# project name carries an install id, the paths are that box's paths, and it is
# regenerated by the gate that needs it.
#
# It also RESOLVES SECRETS. `compose config` interpolates `.env`, so the capture
# holds the database password in plaintext ("PASSWORD": "..." on every service)
# -- on the 2026-09-02 capture that was the default `password`, but on any real
# install it is the generated one. Nothing of this shape belongs in the repo.
#
# Not `pylauncher/build/` wholesale: `pylauncher.spec` and
# `check-bundle-closure.sh` are tracked there. Checked with
# `git log --all -- 'pylauncher/build/gate-*.json'` before adding: never tracked
# on any branch.
pylauncher/build/gate-*.json

# Byte-code from running a gate harness in place. `pylauncher/.gitignore` has
# covered its own tree since the start; `pyplan/gates/` holds runnable scripts
# too, and importing one leaves a `__pycache__` beside it (2026-09-04).
__pycache__/
